§§ `ss 73(3), 74(3), 74A(4), 74B(4), 74C(4), 74D(4) - the courts' jurisdiction over the enhanced punishments`

-- Each of the six subsections says, "despite anything to the contrary in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010", that a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction to try the offences
-- to which the section applies "where no imprisonment is prescribed or where twice the maximum term of imprisonment prescribed for the offence does not exceed 5 years", and
-- power to impose the full punishment provided under the section's enhancing subsection; and that a District Court has jurisdiction to try them and power to impose the full punishment.
-- One helper reads the punishment prescribed for the offence, as a `Punishment` record, for the Magistrate's Court; the six subsections use it (FORK DEF-M2: the
-- "where" is read as limiting the Magistrate's Court's power to impose the full punishment as well as its jurisdiction, as 73(3)(a) and 74A(4)(a) put them in one sentence).
-- Whether the offence is within the section ("the offences in subsection (1)", "specified in subsection (2)", and so on) is an input of each wrapper, not wired to
-- `enhanced penalty under s 73` and its siblings in pc-general-part.l4: for s 73 that function also folds in the exception in subsection (2), and for s 74 the
-- aggravation of subsection (4), which the jurisdiction subsections do not mention (FORK DEF-M7; the same comparison was not made for ss 74A to 74D).
-- src:2154 | (3) Despite anything to the contrary in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 —
-- src:2156 | (a) a Magistrate’s Court has jurisdiction to try the offences in subsection (1),
-- src:2157 | where no imprisonment is prescribed or where twice the maximum term of
-- src:2158 | imprisonment prescribed for the offence does not exceed 5 years, and has
-- src:2159 | power to impose the full punishment provided under that subsection in
-- src:2160 | respect of those offences; and
-- src:2162 | (b) a District Court has jurisdiction to try the offences in subsection (1) and
-- src:2163 | has power to impose the full punishment provided under that subsection in
-- src:2164 | respect of those offences.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 73(3) (src:2154-2164)
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 73(3) (src:2154-2160)
@export Whether a Magistrate's Court may try an offence and impose the full punishment on the footing of the punishment prescribed for the offence: where no imprisonment is prescribed, or twice the maximum term of imprisonment prescribed does not exceed 5 years (the condition in sections 73(3)(a), 74(3)(a)(i), 74A(4)(a), 74B(4)(a), 74C(4)(a) and 74D(4)(a) of the Penal Code 1871); NOTHING otherwise, and where the prescribed imprisonment is for life or has no stated maximum
GIVEN p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment the offence's own section prescribes
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a Magistrate's Court's jurisdiction on the punishment prescribed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `prescribed at all` (p's `imprisonment for life`)
        THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where no imprisonment is prescribed or where twice the maximum term ... does not exceed 5 years": imprisonment for life is prescribed and has no maximum term to double; the grant is limited by its own wording, so the Court is not said to lack jurisdiction (marginal reading b)
        IF NOT (`prescribed at all` (p's imprisonment))
        THEN JUST TRUE
            -- the text's own "where no imprisonment is prescribed" (death alone, or a fine alone, is no imprisonment); NOT is the whole of this condition, so there is no precedence to trip over
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER p's `maximum term in months`
            WHEN JUST m THEN
                IF 2 * m AT MOST 60
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING
                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): twice the maximum term exceeds 5 years; the grant is limited by its own wording, so the Court is not said to lack jurisdiction (marginal reading b)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section prescribes imprisonment but states no maximum, so twice the maximum cannot be compared with 5 years

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 73(3) (src:2154-2160)
@export Whether a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction to try the offences in section 73(1) and power to impose the full punishment provided under that subsection (section 73(3)(a) of the Penal Code 1871); NOTHING where the offence is not one of them
GIVEN `the offence is one of the offences in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one of the offences in section 73(1): an offence under the Code, other than an excluded offence, committed against a domestic worker by an employer, a member of the employer's household or an employment agent?
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment the offence's own section prescribes
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(3)(a) a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the offence is one of the offences in subsection (1)`
    THEN `a Magistrate's Court's jurisdiction on the punishment prescribed` p
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 73(3) speaks of the offences in section 73(1)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 73(3) (src:2162-2164)
@export Whether a District Court has jurisdiction to try the offences in section 73(1) and power to impose the full punishment provided under that subsection (section 73(3)(b) of the Penal Code 1871); NOTHING where the offence is not one of them
GIVEN `the offence is one of the offences in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one of the offences in section 73(1)?
